{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Nested routing means that routes can be nested within other routes, including the way they render. So how do we tell our routes where to render this nested content?"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-outlet-component","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Outlet"},{"type":"text","value":" Component"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Outlet"},{"type":"text","value":" component is used to render the next potentially matching child route. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<Outlet />"},{"type":"text","value":" doesn't take any props and can be rendered anywhere within a route's component tree. If there is no matching child route, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<Outlet />"},{"type":"text","value":" will render "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"callout","kind":"tip","title":"Tip","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If a route's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"component"},{"type":"text","value":" is left undefined, it will render an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<Outlet />"},{"type":"text","value":" automatically."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A great example is configuring the root route of your application. Let's give our root route a component that renders a title, then an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<Outlet />"},{"type":"text","value":" for our top-level routes to render."}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { createRootRoute, Outlet } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createRootRoute({\n  component: RootComponent,\n})\n\nfunction RootComponent() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>My App</h1>\n      <Outlet /> {/* This is where child routes will render */}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { createRootRoute, Outlet } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nexport const Route = createRootRoute({\n  component: RootComponent,\n})\n\nfunction RootComponent() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>My App</h1>\n      <Outlet /> {/* This is where child routes will render */}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import { createRootRoute, Outlet } from '@tanstack/react-router'\\n\\nexport const Route = createRootRoute({\\n  component: RootComponent,\\n})\\n\\nfunction RootComponent() {\\n  return (\\n    <div>\\n      <h1>My App</h1>\\n      <Outlet /> {/* This is where child routes will render */}\\n    </div>\\n  )\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import { createRootRoute, Outlet } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\\n\\nexport const Route = createRootRoute({\\n  component: RootComponent,\\n})\\n\\nfunction RootComponent() {\\n  return (\\n    <div>\\n      <h1>My App</h1>\\n      <Outlet /> {/* This is where child routes will render */}\\n    </div>\\n  )\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}}],"headings":[{"id":"the-outlet-component","text":"The Outlet Component","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","solid"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nNested routing means that routes can be nested within other routes, including the way they render. So how do we tell our routes where to render this nested content?\n\n## The `Outlet` Component\n\nThe `Outlet` component is used to render the next potentially matching child route. `<Outlet />` doesn't take any props and can be rendered anywhere within a route's component tree. If there is no matching child route, `<Outlet />` will render `null`.\n\n> [!TIP]\n> If a route's `component` is left undefined, it will render an `<Outlet />` automatically.\n\nA great example is configuring the root route of your application. Let's give our root route a component that renders a title, then an `<Outlet />` for our top-level routes to render.\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx\nimport { createRootRoute, Outlet } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createRootRoute({\n  component: RootComponent,\n})\n\nfunction RootComponent() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>My App</h1>\n      <Outlet /> {/* This is where child routes will render */}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx\nimport { createRootRoute, Outlet } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nexport const Route = createRootRoute({\n  component: RootComponent,\n})\n\nfunction RootComponent() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>My App</h1>\n      <Outlet /> {/* This is where child routes will render */}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Outlets\n---\n\nNested routing means that routes can be nested within other routes, including the way they render. So how do we tell our routes where to render this nested content?\n\n## The `Outlet` Component\n\nThe `Outlet` component is used to render the next potentially matching child route. `<Outlet />` doesn't take any props and can be rendered anywhere within a route's component tree. If there is no matching child route, `<Outlet />` will render `null`.\n\n> [!TIP]\n> If a route's `component` is left undefined, it will render an `<Outlet />` automatically.\n\nA great example is configuring the root route of your application. Let's give our root route a component that renders a title, then an `<Outlet />` for our top-level routes to render.\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx\nimport { createRootRoute, Outlet } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createRootRoute({\n  component: RootComponent,\n})\n\nfunction RootComponent() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>My App</h1>\n      <Outlet /> {/* This is where child routes will render */}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx\nimport { createRootRoute, Outlet } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nexport const Route = createRootRoute({\n  component: RootComponent,\n})\n\nfunction RootComponent() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>My App</h1>\n      <Outlet /> {/* This is where child routes will render */}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n"}
